    "notes": "Shared campus Q192988 plus unique way268533442/native35184640622274, the mapped cross-shaped South Building. Parent has no mapped height and no contained building_part records in this extract. Own anchor raw[59.5,110], X east/Z south, heading0 baked into the mapped footprint. East/west photo labels and cross arms guide orientation. Four repeated roof/stack treatments and hidden north/south elevations are reconstructed; lower west service-door assignment is approximate. Only this parent footprint is owned; the separately mapped planetarium and every other campus building remain independent. Existing standard Protomaps20261020/Mapzen201x201/6m Observatory extract reused. Uncovered western approach internal[-16.8,0] fixes datum44.36029666666667m, working lower floor0.6m above it with three0.2m treads. Original hill slopes across the cross-shaped footprint; closed foundation follows its minimum boundary grade. Only the occupied parent footprint cuts ground. Approximate native exterior fit reviewed on the original hill; boundary grades -0.257..+1.332m leave a modest lower-side base and slight uphill burial. Exact historic retaining terraces, principal first-floor access and thresholds remain approximate. No bespoke terrain acquisition or broad flattening."
